<% content_for(:title, "ForgeCI — CircleCI-compatible CI/CD you run yourself") %>

<section class="lp-hero">
  <div class="lp-hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-hero-layout">
      <div>
        <a class="lp-tag" href="https://github.com/azmi2409/forge-ci"><b>MIT</b>Open source and self-hosted</a>
        <h1 class="lp-display">Your CircleCI config. <span class="dim">Your runners.</span></h1>
        <p class="lp-lede">
          ForgeCI runs your existing <strong>.circleci/config.yml</strong> on machines you control. Push to GitHub and
          Docker runners pick up the jobs, stream the logs live and report back to the pull request.
        </p>
        <div class="lp-hero-actions">
          <a class="lp-btn" href="#quickstart">Get started<span class="lp-btn-icon"><%= icon "arrow-right" %></span></a>
          <a class="lp-btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/azmi2409/forge-ci"><%= icon "github" %>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-stage" aria-label="Example config">
        <div class="lp-stage-head"><span class="lp-mono">.circleci/config.yml</span><span class="lp-mono">v2.1</span></div>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c"># The config you already have.</span>
<span class="k">version</span>: 2.1

<span class="k">jobs</span>:
  <span class="k">test</span>:
    <span class="k">docker</span>:
      - <span class="k">image</span>: cimg/ruby:3.3
    <span class="k">resource_class</span>: spot
    <span class="k">parallelism</span>: 4
    <span class="k">steps</span>:
      - checkout
      - <span class="k">run</span>: bundle install
      - <span class="k">run</span>: |
          circleci tests glob "test/**/*_test.rb" |
            circleci tests run --split-by=filesize \
              --command="xargs bin/rails test"

<span class="k">workflows</span>:
  <span class="k">ci</span>:
    <span class="k">jobs</span>: [test]</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="lp-facts">
      <div><dt>Config</dt><dd>CircleCI 2.1</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Runners</dt><dd>Outbound only</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Built with</dt><dd>Ruby + Rails</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Per-minute fees</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section" id="features">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-head">
      <p class="lp-mono">Features</p>
      <h2>What you use in CircleCI. <span class="dim">On your hardware.</span></h2>
      <p>A Rails control plane, a pure-Ruby config compiler and zero-dependency Docker runners.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-bento">
      <article class="lp-card">
        <p class="lp-card-label">Config</p>
        <h3>Bring the config you have.</h3>
        <p>Executors, commands, parameters, workflows, <code>requires</code>, <code>matrix</code>, branch filters and contexts. The compiler follows CircleCI's own compile rules.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <p class="lp-card-label">Runners</p>
        <h3>Run jobs anywhere.</h3>
        <p>Runners poll over outbound HTTPS, so they work behind NAT. Route jobs with <code>resource_class</code>: checks on Spot instances, deploys on an on-demand host.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <p class="lp-card-label">Tests</p>
        <h3>Split the suite.</h3>
        <p><code>parallelism: 4</code> and <code>circleci tests run</code> give each runner a share of the files, balanced by size.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <p class="lp-card-label">Logs</p>
        <h3>Watch it live.</h3>
        <p>Step output streams to the dashboard as it runs, with secrets masked before they leave the runner.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <p class="lp-card-label">GitHub</p>
        <h3>Report to the pull request.</h3>
        <p>A GitHub App starts pipelines on push and pull request, clones private repos with short-lived tokens and posts commit statuses.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-head">
      <p class="lp-mono">How it works</p>
      <h2>From push to a green check. <span class="dim">Three steps.</span></h2>
      <p>No inbound ports on your runners and no hosted control plane.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="lp-steps">
      <li><span class="lp-mono">01</span><h3>Push</h3><p>The GitHub App gets the webhook and reads <code>.circleci/config.yml</code> at that commit. Without the App, start a run from any script with <code>forge-ci trigger</code>.</p></li>
      <li><span class="lp-mono">02</span><h3>Compile</h3><p>The config is validated and compiled into workflows and jobs. A config with errors fails fast, with the error on the commit.</p></li>
      <li><span class="lp-mono">03</span><h3>Run</h3><p>Runners claim queued jobs, run each step in Docker and stream logs back. A job starts as soon as the jobs it requires pass.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section" id="compatibility">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-head">
      <p class="lp-mono">Compatibility</p>
      <h2>What works today. <span class="dim">What doesn't yet.</span></h2>
      <p>An unsupported feature fails with a clear error instead of running differently.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="compat">
      <div>
        <p class="lp-card-label" style="margin-bottom: 13px">Supported</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="yes"><%= icon "check" %><span>Docker executors and service containers, <code>executors</code>, <code>commands</code>, parameters</span></li>
          <li class="yes"><%= icon "check" %><span>Workflows, <code>requires</code>, <code>matrix</code>, branch filters, contexts</span></li>
          <li class="yes"><%= icon "check" %><span>Caches, workspaces, artifacts, <code>when</code> conditions, timeouts</span></li>
          <li class="yes"><%= icon "check" %><span><code>parallelism</code> with <code>circleci tests glob</code>, <code>split</code> and <code>run</code></span></li>
          <li class="yes"><%= icon "check" %><span>Bash steps, <code>$BASH_ENV</code> and <code>CIRCLE_*</code> variables</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lp-card-label" style="margin-bottom: 13px">Not yet</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="no"><%= icon "close" %><span>Orbs, because there is no orb registry yet</span></li>
          <li class="no"><%= icon "close" %><span><code>machine</code>, <code>macos</code> and <code>windows</code> executors</span></li>
          <li class="no"><%= icon "close" %><span>Approval jobs, dynamic config and scheduled pipelines</span></li>
          <li class="no"><%= icon "close" %><span>Splitting by timings</span></li>
          <li class="no"><%= icon "close" %><span>Docker layer caching and SSH re-runs</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section" id="quickstart">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-head">
      <p class="lp-mono">Quickstart</p>
      <h2>Running in five minutes. <span class="dim">One compose file.</span></h2>
      <p>Postgres, the control plane, the worker and a runner.</p>
    </div>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="p">$ </span>git clone https://github.com/azmi2409/forge-ci &amp;&amp; cd forge-ci
<span class="p">$ </span>cp .env.example .env          <span class="c"># S3 bucket and credentials, secrets</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>openssl rand -hex 32          <span class="c"># paste into .env as RUNNER_TOKEN</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>docker compose up --build -d
<span class="p">$ </span>docker compose up -d runner
<span class="c"># then open http://localhost:3000 and sign in</span></code></pre>
    <p class="note">Create the S3 bucket first with <code>aws s3 mb s3://&lt;bucket&gt;</code>. For production, with HTTPS, the GitHub App and runners on their own hosts, follow the <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/azmi2409/forge-ci/blob/main/DEPLOY.md">deploy guide</a>.</p>

    <div class="lp-cta">
      <div class="lp-cta-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <svg class="lp-cta-mark" viewBox="6 5 20 21" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 18.5h13.5c0 2.2-1.8 4-4 4H15l1 2.5h-6l1-2.5c-1.7 0-3-1.3-3-3v-1z"/><path d="M18.6 6.5l-3.1 6.2h3l-2 4.3 5.6-6.4h-3.1l2.3-4.1z"/></svg>
      <p class="lp-mono">Open source</p>
      <h2>Stop paying per minute.</h2>
      <p>Point ForgeCI at the config you have and run it on hardware you already own.</p>
      <a class="lp-btn" href="https://github.com/azmi2409/forge-ci">Get ForgeCI on GitHub<span class="lp-btn-icon"><%= icon "arrow-right" %></span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
